(1347430, 170305, 28464, '<td valign="top">Great shot! Slight ccw tilt about 1-2 degrees ..  The chromatic abberation on the right is a little distracting - often caused by adding a  magnifier filter to the camera. Obviously there was a very shallow DOF as I would have liked to have seen the Japan Mov ..... words clear as well..  But I am going to bump you up - good job 8</td>', 'Great shot! Slight ccw tilt about 1-2 degrees ..  The chromatic abberation on the right is a little distracting - often caused by adding a  magnifier filter to the camera. Obviously there was a very shallow DOF as I would have liked to have seen the Japan Mov ..... words clear as well..  But I am going to bump you up - good job 8', '2005-04-30 19:06:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(1347441, 170172, 28464, '<td valign="top">Nice Job! I would have considered cropping out more of the hair (part line is a bit distracting) and keeping more of her chin - as she seems a little cut off. I love the sharpening on the earring. I may have considered cloning out the wrinkles by her eye (I am not sure even if that would be allowed or not - but I do not think it''s a major element in this photo) The background color change is distracting  from her eye on down  - about 1/2" strip - I think I would have cloned that to match the other. Beautiful girl - good choice. I think the teeth could have been dodged (or differently as I think some dodging was done) to eliminate the darker lower part on ther fron teeth. An eyelash brush could have helped.  Depending on which monitor I look at the photo seems a little washed - not sure what it would have looked like if it were slightly darker. Bumping up  8</td>', 'Nice Job! I would have considered cropping out more of the hair (part line is a bit distracting) and keeping more of her chin - as she seems a little cut off. I love the sharpening on the earring. I may have considered cloning out the wrinkles by her eye (I am not sure even if that would be allowed or not - but I do not think it''s a major element in this photo) The background color change is distracting  from her eye on down  - about 1/2" strip - I think I would have cloned that to match the other. Beautiful girl - good choice. I think the teeth could have been dodged (or differently as I think some dodging was done) to eliminate the darker lower part on ther fron teeth. An eyelash brush could have helped.  Depending on which monitor I look at the photo seems a little washed - not sure what it would have looked like if it were slightly darker. Bumping up  8', '2005-04-30 19:16:13.000000', NULL, 1),
